{% import "partials/copy-command.njk" as cmd %}
{% import "partials/zoomable-image.njk" as media %}

<h1>Adding endpoints</h1>
<p>Register an endpoint so the controller can distribute test packages and execute steps on it.</p>

<h2 id="install-endpoint">Install the endpoint</h2>
<p>If the endpoint machine is connected to the internet, install it the same way as the controller:</p>
{{ cmd.copyCommand("pip install orcraft") }}
<p>If it is not connected, download the wheel file instead and install it directly:</p>
{{ cmd.copyCommand("pip install orcraft-<version>-py3-none-any.whl") }}

<h2 id="run-endpoint">Run the endpoint</h2>

<h3 id="insecure-endpoint-connection">Insecure endpoint connection</h3>
<p>For a fast setup on a trusted local network, the endpoint can be run without security enabled:</p>
{{ cmd.copyCommand("orcraft-endpoint run -secure disabled") }}

<h3 id="secure-endpoint-connection">Secure endpoint connection</h3>
<p>For a secure deployment, follow the security setup procedure in the controller's Security tab:</p>
{{ media.zoomableImage("/assets/images/screenshots/setup-security-tab.png", "The controller's Security tab, used to generate the authorization token and certificates") }}
<p>Once that's done, run the endpoint with authentication enabled, which is the default:</p>
{{ cmd.copyCommand("orcraft-endpoint run") }}
